Here is a concise report based on the repo at `/home/admin`.

---

## 1. Frontend: teacher / director assessment UI

**Main page**

- **`/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/LearningRecordsPage.vue`** — Routed from `App.vue` when `active === 'learning'` (props: `branch-id`, `user-role`, `user-id`, `target-record-id`). Teachers see「我的課表 & 評量」with the week/today schedule and tabs (全部 / 待審核 / 需修改 / 已核准); directors see「學習評量表」with review tabs and filters.

```1:7:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/LearningRecordsPage.vue
<template>
  <div class="lr-page">
    <!-- Page Header -->
    <div class="page-header lr-header" data-guide="learning-header">
      <div>
        <h2>{{ isTeacher ? '我的課表 & 評量' : '學習評量表' }}</h2>
        <p class="page-desc">{{ isTeacher ? '查看本週課表，填寫學習評量' : '查看、新增與審核學生每堂課的學習評量' }}</p>
```

**Related views**

- **`/home/admin/frontend/src/App.vue`** — Imports and renders `LearningRecordsPage` for the learning tab.
- **`/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue`** — Course-side「評量表紀錄」and `GET /api/v1/learning-records?student_class_id=...` for eval records on a course.
- **`/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/ParentPortal.vue`** — Parent-facing「學習評量」(approved records via parent dashboard API, not the same as the staff list).
- **`/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/TeacherHomePage.vue`** — Fetches learning records for pending/overdue widgets (e.g. `per_page: 200` without a date range on the main fetch).
- **`/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/DirectorDashboard.vue`** — Uses `learning-records` with `status=pending,changes_requested&per_page=100`.

---

## 2. Date filtering (list): defaults and query params

**Staff list (`LearningRecordsPage.vue`)**

- Filter state: `filters = { status, student_name, teacher_id, date }` with **`date` default `''`** (no range).

```781:781:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/LearningRecordsPage.vue
const filters = reactive({ status: '', student_name: '', teacher_id: '', date: '' });
```

- **`_buildRecordsParams`** only sends **`start_date` and `end_date` when `filters.date` is set**, and sets **both to the same day** (single-day filter). There is **no built-in “last 2 months” (or any default window)** on initial load.

```1746:1756:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/LearningRecordsPage.vue
const _buildRecordsParams = (page = 1) => {
  const params = new URLSearchParams();
  if (props.branchId) params.set('branch_id', props.branchId);
  if (filters.student_name) params.set('student_name', filters.student_name);
  if (filters.teacher_id) params.set('teacher_id', filters.teacher_id);
  if (filters.status) params.set('status', filters.status);
  if (filters.date) { params.set('start_date', filters.date); params.set('end_date', filters.date); }
  params.set('sort', 'session_date');
  params.set('per_page', String(perfFlags.LR_DEFAULT_PER_PAGE));
  params.set('page', String(page));
  return params;
};
```

- **Pagination**, not a calendar cutoff, is what limits how many rows load at once: **`LR_DEFAULT_PER_PAGE` is 50** (`/home/admin/frontend/src/lib/perfFlags.js`). Older rows are still in the dataset; users need **「載入更多」** (`loadMoreRecords`) to pull additional pages.

**Backend (`LearningRecordController@index`)**

- Applies `SessionDate >= start_date` / `SessionDate <= end_date` **only if those query params are present**; optional `only_due` filters to sessions whose end time is already past (not used by `LearningRecordsPage`’s `_buildRecordsParams`).

```157:179:/home/admin/backend/app/Http/Controllers/LearningRecordController.php
        if ($request->filled('start_date')) {
            $query->where('SessionDate', '>=', $request->input('start_date'));
        }
        if ($request->filled('end_date')) {
            $query->where('SessionDate', '<=', $request->input('end_date'));
        }

        // Optional: only return records whose class session has already ended.
        // Useful for dashboard "pending review" cards to avoid future classes.
        if ($request->boolean('only_due', false)) {
            $now = Carbon::now()->format('Y-m-d H:i:s');
            $query->whereRaw("CONCAT(SessionDate, ' ', COALESCE(EndTime, '23:59:59')) <= ?", [$now]);
        }
        ...
        $records = $query->with('studentClass.student')
            ->orderBy('SessionDate', 'desc')
            ->orderBy('id', 'desc')
            ->paginate($perPage);
```

Note: the frontend sends `sort=session_date`, but **`index` does not read it**; ordering is fixed as above.

**Parent dashboard (different behavior)**

- **`/home/admin/backend/app/Http/Controllers/ParentPortalController.php`**: learning records are **approved-only**, ordered by **`ApprovedAt` desc**, paginated with **`lr_page` / `lr_per_page`** (default per_page 10, capped 50). **No date filter** on that query—history is limited by pagination, not by “last N months.”

```270:285:/home/admin/backend/app/Http/Controllers/ParentPortalController.php
        // Learning records (approved only) — paginated
        $lrPage    = max(1, (int) $request->query('lr_page', 1));
        $lrPerPage = min(50, max(5, (int) $request->query('lr_per_page', 10)));
        ...
            $recordsRaw = $lrQuery
                ->orderBy('ApprovedAt', 'desc')
                ->skip(($lrPage - 1) * $lrPerPage)
                ->take($lrPerPage)
                ->get();
```

---

## 3. Subject (科目) grouping in the assessment views

**`LearningRecordsPage.vue` (teachers / directors)**

- The main table is **grouped by student**, not by subject. Each row shows **科目** from `student_class_label` (resolved subject name from `StudentClass` → `Subject`) or fallback `Subject`.

```797:831:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/LearningRecordsPage.vue
const groupedRecordsByStudent = computed(() => {
  const groups = new Map();
  for (const record of records.value || []) {
    const studentId = Number(record?.student_id || 0) || null;
    const studentName = String(record?.student_name || '').trim() || '未命名學生';
    const key = studentId ? `student-${studentId}` : `name-${studentName}`;
    ...
```

So **multiple subjects for one student appear in the same accordion group**, sorted by session date/time—not separate subject sections.

**`ParentPortal.vue`**

- Here, **subject grouping is client-side**: records are grouped by a subject key; if more than one subject exists, a **filter row** lets parents pick one subject.

```537:560:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/ParentPortal.vue
const recordSubjectKey = (record) => {
  const raw = record?.Subject ?? record?.subject ?? record?.SubjectName ?? '';
  const key = String(raw).trim();
  return key || '其他';
};

const learningRecordsBySubject = computed(() => {
  const groups = new Map();
  for (const record of allLearningRecords.value) {
    const key = recordSubjectKey(record);
    if (!groups.has(key)) groups.set(key, []);
    groups.get(key).push(record);
  }
  return Array.from(groups.entries()).sort((a, b) =>
    a[0].localeCompare(b[0], 'zh-Hant-TW')
  );
});

const visibleLearningRecordGroups = computed(() => {
  const all = learningRecordsBySubject.value;
  const f = String(lrSubjectFilter.value || '').trim();
  if (!f) return all;
  return all.filter(([subj]) => subj === f);
});
```

---

## 4. API routes for learning records / per-student usage

Defined in **`/home/admin/backend/routes/api.php`** (authenticated group):

- **`GET /api/v1/learning-records`** — list (paginated), main list for `LearningRecordsPage`.
- **`POST /api/v1/learning-records`** — create.
- **`PUT|POST /api/v1/learning-records/{learningRecord}`** — update.
- **`DELETE /api/v1/learning-records/{learningRecord}`** — destroy.
- Approvals / batch / reschedule / ensure-past, etc., on the same prefix.

**“Per student” on the list API** is done via:

- **`student_name`** (LIKE match → student → `StudentClassID`s), or  
- **`student_class_id`** / **`student_class_ids`**,  

not a dedicated `student_id` query on `index` (the controller hydrates `student_id` on each row for the response).

**Parents (single student from session + optional sibling switch)**

- **`GET /api/v1/parent/dashboard`** — returns `learning_records` + `learning_records_meta` for that student.

---

## 5. Backend controller

- **`/home/admin/backend/app/Http/Controllers/LearningRecordController.php`** — `index`, `store`, `update`, `approve`, `reject`, batch ops, `ensurePastRecords`, etc. The **`index`** method (lines 49–216 in the file read) is the one that powers the staff assessment list.

---

### Quick answers to your numbered questions

| Question | Answer |
|----------|--------|
| Teacher assessment pages | Primary: `LearningRecordsPage.vue`; related: `SmartCalendar.vue`, `TeacherHomePage.vue`, `DirectorDashboard.vue`, `ParentPortal.vue` (parents). |
| Default date hiding old rows? | **No default date range.** Empty `filters.date` → no `start_date`/`end_date`. **50 rows per page** can hide older data until **載入更多**. |
| Subjects mixed vs separated | **Staff page: by student (subjects mixed in one group).** **Parent portal: grouped by subject** with optional subject filter when multiple. |
| Fetch assessments per student | Staff: **`GET /api/v1/learning-records`** with `student_name` or `student_class_id(s)` (+ `branch_id` as needed). Parents: **`GET /api/v1/parent/dashboard`** with `lr_page` / `lr_per_page`. |

